  "response_text": "It is important to be aware of warning signs that a relationship may be unsafe, especially when it comes to setting boundaries with family members. Here are some signs to watch for:\n\n  1. Feeling threatened or intimidated by family members.\n  2. Being controlled or manipulated by family members.\n  3. Being excluded from important family decisions or events.\n  4. Feeling unsafe or in danger when around family members.\n  5. Being forced to do things that go against your values or beliefs.\n  6. Being isolated from friends and social activities.\n  7. Feeling like you have no control over your life or future.\n  8. Being in a toxic or abusive relationship with family members.\n\nIf you are experiencing any of these warning signs, it is important to seek help from a trusted friend, family member, or professional. It is also important to consider your safety and take steps to protect yourself, such as seeking a safe place to stay or contacting a crisis hotline.",
